No, you can never become neutral by wearing a [HoOA.  To be neutral you
have to convert.  In order to convert, you need the following 3 things:

1) A neutral altar.
2) A negative alignment.
3) A sacrifice-able corpse that is not of your own race.
 - 2 and 3 can be combined together by using a co-aligned unicorn
corpse
 - Do NOT convert before being accepted on your quest if you ever want
to ascend.

After you convert, you will probably want to correct your luck and
alignment, which will require many sacrifices.  You would also need to
re-purchase protection.  You will be unable to convert again, but
neutral characters can use a [HoOA to become lawful or chaotic.  Note
that using a [HoOA will also remove any protection you have received.

The Eye of the Aethiopica is the Wizard's quest artifact.  It is an
amulet of ESP which provides MR, 1/2 spell damage, and Pw regeneration
when carried.  It can be invoked to provide instant transportation to
any of the dungeon branches that you have visited.

Note, after you convert, most of your old chaotic artifacts will blast
you when you use (wield, apply, invoke, pick up, take out of a
container) them.

Once you are neutral, after you have wished for and received the "EotA,
you could continue sacrificing for artifacts.  Magicbane's curse
absorbsion and Elbereth-engraving abilities are very helpful, and some
players feel it is dangerous to face the Astral Plane if the Vorpal
Blade hasn't been created yet.  Note that with so many artifacts
already existing, this might take forever.  It would have been a sure
thing to get )VB if you had not been crowned yet, however.

When you are going around in human form, you might want to wear a
shield of reflection, despite the penalties.  You might also want to
obtain a robe of power, to improve your spellcasting.

